# Content Management and MDX Guidelines

Rules for managing content and using MDX in the ONE framework.

## Content Collections

### Structure
- Organize content in `src/content/` directory.
- Group related content in collections (e.g., `blog`, `docs`, `prompts`).
- Use consistent file naming conventions.

### Frontmatter
- Include required metadata in frontmatter:
  - `title`: The content title
  - `description`: A brief description
  - `date`: Publication date (YYYY-MM-DD format)
  - `section`: Content section or category
  - `order`: Numerical order for sorting (if applicable)

### Example
```markdown
---
title: Getting Started
description: Learn how to get started with ONE framework
date: 2024-02-01
section: Introduction
order: 1
---

# Getting Started with ONE

Content goes here...
```

## MDX Usage

### Components in MDX
- Import components at the top of the MDX file.
- Use components with proper props.
- Keep component usage simple and focused.

### Example
```mdx
---
title: Interactive Guide
layout: ../layouts/DocsLayout.astro
---

import { Tabs, TabItem } from '@/components/ui/tabs';
import { Alert } from '@/components/ui/alert';

# Interactive Guide

<Alert variant="info">
  This guide includes interactive examples.
</Alert>

<Tabs>
  <TabItem value="react" label="React">
    React content here...
  </TabItem>
  <TabItem value="astro" label="Astro">
    Astro content here...
  </TabItem>
</Tabs>
```

## Content Formatting

### Headings
- Use proper heading hierarchy (h1 → h2 → h3).
- Include only one h1 per page.
- Keep headings concise and descriptive.

### Lists
- Use unordered lists for items without sequence.
- Use ordered lists for sequential steps.
- Maintain consistent formatting.

### Code Blocks
- Specify the language for syntax highlighting.
- Use proper indentation.
- Include comments for complex code.

```tsx
// Example React component
const Example = () => {
  return <div>Example</div>;
};
```

### Links
- Use relative links for internal navigation.
- Use descriptive link text.
- Include title attributes for accessibility.

## Images and Media

### Image Usage
- Store images in `public/images/` or use content collections.
- Include alt text for all images.
- Optimize images for web.
- Use responsive images when appropriate.

### Example
```markdown
![Dashboard overview with key metrics](../../public/images/dashboard.png)
```

## Chat Configuration

### System Prompts
- Define clear system prompts for AI assistants.
- Structure prompts with clear sections.
- Include examples when helpful.

### Example
```yaml
chatConfig:
  systemPrompt:
    - type: text
      text: "You are an expert in [topic] focused on helping visitors understand [specific aspects]."
  welcome:
    message: "👋 How can I help you with [topic]?"
    suggestions:
      - label: "Getting Started"
        prompt: "How do I get started with [topic]?"
```

## Best Practices
- Keep content focused and concise.
- Use consistent terminology throughout.
- Include examples and code snippets when helpful.
- Maintain a clear information hierarchy.
- Test content rendering in both light and dark modes. 